         Online Payment Center Order Birth, Marriage, Death Certificates; Pay for Dog Licenses, Late Fees; Order Documents Office Hours: Monday, Tuesday, Thursday 8:30 am to 2 pm, Tuesday Evenings 5 pm to 7 pm, Wednesday 8:30 am to 12 pm The Town Clerk is elected every three years. The Town Clerk is: Chief Election Official: Oversees all elections, voter registration sessions, certifies nomination papers, initiative petitions and conducts annual town census Recording Officer: Records, certifies and maintains all official actions of the town Registry of Vital Statistics: Registers all birth, marriage, and death records occurring within the community Public Records Officer: Administers the oath of office to all elected and appointed members. Posts all meetings of government bodies. Provides certified copies of vital records.Maintains records of all local bylaws Licensing Officer: Issues licenses and permits: marriage, dog, and permits for raffles and bazaars Public Information Officer: Responds to inquiries from the general public on information available through the officer ALL ELECTIONS ARE HELD AT 29 FOREST ST., SENIOR CENTER Annual Town Election:  Held the first Monday of May from 7 am to 8 pm at the Senior Center located at 29 Forest Street. Annual Town Meeting:  Held the second Friday of June at 7:30 pm in the Elementary School Auditorium. 
     

 
